cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LLM-MovieLens: A Portable Pipeline and Testbed for LLM-Synthesized Item Profiles"
message: >-
  If you use this resource, please cite the paper. The DOI below is the concept
  DOI, which always resolves to the newest release; each release also has its own
  version DOI, listed on the Zenodo record — v1.0's is 10.5281/zenodo.22766654.
type: dataset
# The RELEASE version, not the CFF schema version above. Kept equal to
# metadata/croissant.json's "version" -- two files naming different versions of
# one artifact is what a reader notices first.
version: "1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Duong
    given-names: Tan Nghia
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2442-6263"
    affiliation: "Hanoi University of Science and Technology; Minastik Technology JSC"
  - family-names: Tran
    given-names: Manh Hoang
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0572-2091"
    affiliation: "Hanoi University of Science and Technology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/minastik-ai/llm-movielens"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/minastik-ai/llm-movielens"
# The CONCEPT DOI: it resolves to the newest version, so a citation made from
# this file aggregates across releases instead of splitting per version. v1.0's
# own DOI is 10.5281/zenodo.22766654, listed on the Zenodo record; it is NOT a
# second `identifiers` entry here, because cffconvert emits that one in
# preference to this field and every generated citation would then split.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22766653"
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
abstract: >-
  Pipeline and evaluation harness for LLM-synthesized item profiles. A language
  model reads an item's structured metadata and writes an 80-120 word profile, a
  10-axis mood vector and 3-5 key themes; the harness evaluates whether the
  resulting representation outperforms the structured description consumed
  directly, under a temporal split, five seeds and full ranking. Code and
  annotations are CC BY 4.0; the generated profiles and their embeddings are
  CC BY-NC 4.0, reflecting upstream terms.
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - large language models
  - item representation
  - MovieLens
  - resource
